35,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,The survey says four hundred kilos per square metre. That is a hard limit. I am relieved it is not less.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The comments are clear. People return for presence, not objects. The head counts confirm it. Mechanisms drive the numbers.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,The lab has only one person left! Two hundred pieces are waiting. And the volunteers are just the history circle. Who is actually standing in the room?,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,The paperwork shows two openings slipped because condition reports arrived after shipping cut-offs. Transport costs also ate a third of the installation budget.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The joiner’s rate doubled, and bespoke mounts cost per object. Worse, powered displays caused seventeen call-outs, four during opening hours. That is where the budget vanishes.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, the head counts show mechanisms draw crowds. But if the room is packed, the floor bears more weight. I am worried.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, the floor limit is a constraint, not a reason to avoid presence. The data shows empty rooms fail. We must find a way to fit the crowd.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, presence is great, but who cleans the two hundred waiting pieces? The history circle walks the old quarter, they don’t know our gallery.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, that backlog is terrifying. If the lab is stuck, the delivery date slips. I am checking if the transport delays compound this.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, the backlog is a risk, but the maintenance logs show the real drain. Powered displays are where the money goes.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Benjamin, if powered displays cause so many call-outs, the floor might not be the only thing stressed. I am worried about the strain.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, the call-outs are a symptom. The root cause is the absence of live engagement. We need presence, not just static objects.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Benjamin, I hear you, but money is easy to find. People are not! If the lab is empty, the objects rot. Who is actually holding the room together?","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, the transport costs are a huge hidden tax. If we add powered displays, the maintenance backlog will explode. We need to keep the logistics simple.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, exactly. Transport is a known tax, but maintenance is the silent killer. I am glad we are avoiding the powered trap.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I am glad we are avoiding the powered trap. It eases my mind about the floor. I will wait for the candidates.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"I am waiting for the candidates. The data points to live engagement, but I need to see which proposals actually deliver that presence.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,I am ready to see the candidates. I just need to know who is actually standing in the room to keep it safe.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I am ready for the candidates. I just need to see which ones avoid the shipping traps and the maintenance nightmare.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I am ready for the candidates. I just need to see which ones keep the invoices predictable and the joiner’s bill manageable.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
