60,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,I am looking at the floor limit. Candidate D uses overhead rigging. That keeps the weight off the bay. I feel safer with that.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, rigging solves the weight, but the comments demand presence. D is light, not people. I need to see who actually stands in the room.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, you are right. D is just lights. A has craftspeople! But with only one conservator, can we handle the textiles?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, A is local, so no distant shipping cut-offs. That solves my biggest delivery fear. I am leaning toward A.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, local sourcing saves the joiner’s bill. But demonstration tools need maintenance. I am checking if the invoices stay predictable for A.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Rin, the craftspeople in A mean more people in the room. I am worried the floor will feel the extra weight.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, the head counts show crowds follow activity, not just weight. A brings the presence the data demands. I am leaning toward A.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Daisuke, the craftspeople are the point! But with one conservator and a two-hundred-piece backlog, can we even keep the textiles safe? I am worried about the care.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, the local sourcing means no distant shipping delays. That is my main relief. I am leaning toward A, but I need to know if the logistics are simple enough.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, the conservation backlog is a staffing issue, not a budget one. My concern is the joiner’s bill. A’s local tools mean no bespoke mounts, keeping costs predictable.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, I understand the data, but the floor limit is real. I am still anxious about the weight of the crowds.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, the limit is four hundred kilos. A crowd of people is far lighter than the rigging in D. The data says presence wins.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Daisuke, the people are light! The real weight is the work. With one conservator, A is a disaster. C has a visible bench, but who actually sits there?","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, C is local too, so no shipping delays. But a working bench means constant handling. That could worsen the conservation backlog. I am worried about the daily wear.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, exactly. A working bench means constant handling, which means more conservation calls. That is a hidden cost I cannot afford. I am leaning toward A for its predictable invoices.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@Rin, I am sorry, but I cannot ignore the floor. If the crowd is too heavy, the bay fails. I am still anxious.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, the bench in C is a prop, not a service. A offers real presence. The data is clear. I am ready to vote.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, I am ready to vote. A brings the people I need, even if the conservation backlog is terrifying. I just hope the volunteers can help.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Toshio, I agree. A avoids the distant shipping traps that wrecked past seasons. The local logistics are simple and safe. I am ready to vote.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I am ready to vote. Candidate A keeps the joiner’s bill low and avoids the maintenance trap. The invoices will finally make sense.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
